  "answer": {
    "summary": "Implemented buffer lifecycle tracking for ProducerBatch to prevent messages from ending up on the wrong topic by:\n\n1. Added three fields to ProducerBatch:\n   - `inflight`: tracks whether batch is currently in-flight\n   - `bufferDeallocated`: tracks whether buffer has been deallocated  \n   - `expiredDueToDeliveryTimeout`: tracks delivery timeout expiry\n\n2. Added methods to ProducerBatch:\n   - `isInflight()` / `markInflight()` / `clearInflight()`: manage in-flight state\n   - `isBufferDeallocated()` / `markBufferDeallocated()`: manage buffer deallocation state\n   - `markExpiredDueToDeliveryTimeout()` / `isExpiredDueToDeliveryTimeout()`: track expiry reason\n\n3. Updated RecordAccumulator:\n   - Added `completeAndDeallocateBatch()`: marks buffer as deallocated and returns to pool\n   - Added `markBufferAsDeallocated()`: marks buffer as deallocated without returning to pool\n\n4. Updated Sender:\n   - Mark batches as inflight when added to inFlightBatches\n   - Clear inflight flag when removed from inFlightBatches  \n   - Clear inflight flag in getExpiredInflightBatches when batch expires\n   - Track delivery timeout expiry with flag\n   - Use appropriate deallocation method based on failure reason\n\nCurrent test status:\n- RecordAccumulatorTest: ALL PASSING\n- SenderTest: 2 failing (testNoDoubleDeallocation, testCancelInFlightRequestAfterFatalError)\n- testNoBufferReuseWhenBatchExpires: PASSING\n\nThe implementation tracks buffer lifecycle to prevent reuse of expired batch buffers, which could cause messages to be routed to the wrong topic if buffers are mixed between batches."
  },
